{"name":"Fragrant Wand","hex":"#adb1c1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fragrant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sweet-smelling; having a pleasant (usually strong) scent or fragrance.","Attractive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrant"},{"term":"wand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hand-held narrow rod, usually used for pointing or instructing, or as a traditional emblem of authority.","A stick or rod used by a magician (a magic wand), conjurer or diviner (divining rod)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scan (e.g. a passenger at an airport) with a handheld metal detector.","To use a handheld vibrator (the sex toy) on (a person or body part)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fragrance compound","blocks":[{"text":"A fragrance compound is a chemical compound with a pleasant odor. Fragrances affect only the sense of smell, whereas flavors can affect both the sense of taste and smell. Fragrances are often mixtures of individual fragrance compounds. Although many fragrances are derived from natural sources, many are synthetic. Fragrances are widely used in cosmetics and are the basis for a large industry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fragrance_compound"},{"title":"Wand","blocks":[{"text":"A wand is a thin, light-weight rod that is held with one hand, and is traditionally made of wood, but may also be made of other materials, such as metal, bone or stone. Long versions of wands are often styled in forms of staves or sceptres, which could have large ornamentation on the top."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG/330px-John_William_Waterhouse_-_Magic_Circle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wand"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Perfume